# FIL git workflow

Branch flow: **`feature/*` → `dev` → `staging` → production**.

## Feature work

- **New features:** always use a **feature branch** off `dev` — never commit feature work directly to `dev`, `staging`, or `main`/`master`.
- **Create:** `git checkout dev && git pull && git checkout -b feature/<short-name>`
- **When done:** merge feature → `dev` (local merge or PR into `dev`), then delete the feature branch.

## End of day — PR to staging

If GitHub remote is set **and** local `dev` has new commits/merges not on `staging`:

1. `git fetch origin` and compare `dev` to `origin/staging`
2. Push `dev` if needed
3. Open PR **`dev` → `staging`** via `gh pr create --base staging --head dev`

Skip if `dev` is not ahead of `staging` or no GitHub remote.

## Agents

- Offer a feature branch before starting new feature work.
- Merge to `dev` when landing completed work — not directly to `staging`.
- On wrap-up/EOD: check and create staging PR only when conditions above are met.
- Do not force-push protected branches unless explicitly requested.

